# DTO conventions

Three model homes — **do not duplicate** types across them.

## Features (`WebApp/Features/`) — use-case Request / Response

**Canonical pattern:** colocate in the use-case file (see `User/Commands/SignIn.cs`). **Commands and queries** both use `{UseCase}Request` / `{UseCase}Response`; folder and `ICommand<>` / `IQuery<>` distinguish write vs read.

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Message | `{UseCase}Request` | `SignInRequest`, `GetChatThreadsByUserIdRequest` |
| Result | `{UseCase}Response` | `SignInResponse`, `GetChatThreadsByUserIdResponse` |
| Validator | `{UseCase}RequestValidator` | `SignInRequestValidator` |
| Handler | `{UseCase}RequestHandler` | `SignInRequestHandler` |

- Flat **Request** record (primitives) — no wrapper around Core or Models types.
- **Response** at the **bottom** of the same file when the use case owns its result shape.
- Validator targets **Request** directly (`SignInRequestValidator` validates `EmailId`, `Password`).
- Entity → Response mapping lives in handler `#region # Mapping`.

Do **not** put migrated use-case Request/Response in `Core/DTOs/` or `WebApp/Models/`.

## Core (`Core/DTOs/`) — shared port shapes (shrinking)

Types referenced by **`Core/Abstractions/*.cs`** when an entity is not enough. **Prefer entities on ports**; migrate use-case DTOs to Features.

| File | Types (today) |
|------|----------------|
| `ChatThread.cs` | `ChatThreadDto`, add/update/delete thread requests |
| `ChatMessage.cs` | `ChatMessageDto` |
| `General.cs` | `GeneralSettingsDto` |
| `Mail.cs` | Inbox/mailbox types (`InboxQuery`, `MailboxStatusResult`, …) |
| `Foundry.cs` | `FoundryOptions` (bound from `Foundry:` config section) |

Namespace: `Core.DTOs`. Add a file only when a **repository port** needs a shared shape across use cases.

## WebApp (`WebApp/Models/`) — app / UI layer

Types used only by **Features**, Blazor, AI, or endpoints — **not** on `I*Repository` signatures and **not** feature-owned use-case pairs.

| File | Types (today) |
|------|----------------|
| `_Common.cs` | `AppResult`, `AppResult<T>`, `AppError` |
| `Enums.cs` | `ErrorCode`, `SettingsSection` |
| `AI.cs` | `RunChatAgentRequest/Response` |
| `Email.cs` | `EmailSettingsDto` |
| `Constants.cs` | `AuthConstants`, `ChatMessageRoles` |

Namespace: `WebApp.Models`. WebApp `GlobalUsings` imports both `Core.DTOs` and `WebApp.Models`.

## Naming (Core + Models)

| Kind | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Shared projection | `{Entity}Dto` | `ChatThreadDto` |
| App/UI entry (legacy until migrated) | `{Verb}{Entity}Request` / `Response` | `RunChatAgentRequest` |
| UI-only in component | `{Name}ViewModel` in `.razor` `# Types` | not in Models |

Order types in each Core/Models file: **Get Dto → Add/Update requests → Delete request**.

## Layer flow

| Direction | Pattern |
|-----------|---------|
| **UI → Features** | `Sender.SendAsync(new SignInRequest(...))` or form-bound `[FromForm] SignInRequest` |
| **Features → repos** | Primitives and **`Core.Entities`** — not feature Request/Response |
| **Features → caller** | Feature-owned `{UseCase}Response` or legacy `Core.DTOs` / `WebApp.Models` |
| **Repos → Features** | **`Core.Entities`** (target) or legacy `Core.DTOs` projections |

Features validates with `AppResult`; repositories do not take feature Request/Response types.

## Decision tree

1. **Single use-case Request/Response pair?** → `{UseCase}Request` / `{UseCase}Response` in **`WebApp/Features/`** file (commands **and** queries)
2. On an **`I*Repository` method** and shared across use cases? → `Core/DTOs/` (or prefer **`Core/Entities/`** on the port)
3. **`AppResult` shell / AI turn / mailbox UI / unmigrated form DTO**? → `WebApp/Models/`
4. **DB entity**? → `Core/Entities/`
5. **Single-component display state**? → ViewModel in `.razor`

## Example (canonical — SignIn)

```csharp
// User/Commands/SignIn.cs — all in one file
public sealed record SignInRequest(string EmailId, string Password)
    : ICommand<AppResult<SignInResponse>>;

public sealed class SignInRequestHandler(IUserRepository users) : ...
{
    var user = await users.FindActiveByEmailAndPasswordAsync(request.EmailId, request.Password, ct);
    // ...
    private static SignInResponse ToResponse(Core.Entities.User user) => new() { ... };
}

public sealed class SignInResponse { ... }
```

Query (same naming — implements `IQuery<>` instead of `ICommand<>`):

```csharp
// ChatThread/Queries/GetChatThreadsByUserId.cs
public sealed record GetChatThreadsByUserIdRequest(Guid UserId)
    : IQuery<AppResult<GetChatThreadsByUserIdResponse>>;

public sealed class GetChatThreadsByUserIdResponse { ... }
```
